---
const canonicalUrl = 'https://alat.cc/products/ujer/privacy-policy/'
const contactEmail = 'azzam@alat.cc'
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalUrl} />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <meta name="description" content="Privacy Policy for Ujer." />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="alat" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Ujer Privacy Policy — alat" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Privacy Policy for Ujer." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalUrl} />
    <title>Ujer Privacy Policy — alat</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header shell">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="alat home">alat<span>.</span></a>
      <a class="back-link" href="/products/ujer/">← Ujer</a>
    </header>

    <main class="shell policy-page">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Ujer</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: September 16, 2026</p>

      <p class="lead">
        Ujer is a dictation app for Android and macOS. This policy explains
        what information Ujer handles when you use it.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>What Ujer accesses</h2>
        <p>
          Ujer accesses your microphone only after you explicitly start a
          dictation session and grant microphone permission. It does not record
          continuously or in the background.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Audio and transcription</h2>
        <p>
          Ujer records temporary audio locally, then sends that audio to the
          transcription endpoint you configure. Depending on your selected
          provider, this is an OpenAI-compatible
          <code>POST /audio/transcriptions</code> endpoint or Deepgram's
          <code>/listen</code> endpoint. Ujer has no transcription backend of
          its own.
        </p>
        <p>
          The configured provider receives the audio and may process or retain
          it under its own privacy policy and terms. If you use a self-hosted
          endpoint, its operator controls that processing and retention.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>API tokens and settings</h2>
        <p>
          Ujer uses the API token you provide to authenticate transcription
          requests to your configured provider. The token, provider, base URL,
          and model are stored locally on your device. On Android the token is
          encrypted with Android Keystore-backed storage; on macOS it is stored
          in the Keychain. Ujer does not send your token to an Ujer server.
        </p>
        <p>
          Remote endpoints must use HTTPS, except for loopback endpoints used
          for local development.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Transcripts and retention</h2>
        <p>
          Ujer does not maintain an account, cloud sync, voice history, or
          transcript history. Its temporary local audio file is deleted after
          transcription, cancellation, or an error. Transcription providers
          may retain audio or transcripts according to their own policies.
        </p>
        <p>
          Ujer places the transcript in the Android clipboard or inserts it
          into the selected macOS text field. The operating system or another
          app may retain clipboard or inserted text; that retention is outside
          Ujer's control.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What Ujer does not collect</h2>
        <p>
          Ujer does not collect names, email addresses, contacts, location,
          device identifiers, advertising data, or analytics. It has no Ujer
          account system, advertisements, or tracking SDK.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Deleting your information</h2>
        <p>
          You can remove your locally stored API token by clearing it in Ujer's
          settings or uninstalling the app. Temporary audio is deleted
          automatically as described above. To request deletion of data held
          by a transcription provider, contact that provider directly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions or requests, contact
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="shell footer-note">
      <p>Useful software, quietly made.</p>
      <span>alat.cc / 2026</span>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap');
  :global(*) { box-sizing: border-box; }
  :global(body) { background: #151613; color: #f1efe7; font-family: 'Manrope', sans-serif; margin: 0; }
  :global(a) { color: inherit; }
  :global(code) { color: #d7f96a; font: 0.9em 'DM Mono', monospace; }
  .shell { margin: 0 auto; width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 48px)); }
  .site-header { align-items: center; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 30px 0; }
  .wordmark { font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.08em; text-decoration: none; }
  .wordmark span, .eyebrow span { color: #d7f96a; }
  .back-link, .eyebrow, .updated, .footer-note span { color: #85867c; font: 0.68rem 'DM Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .back-link { text-decoration: none; }
  .back-link:hover, a:hover { color: #d7f96a; }
  .policy-page { max-width: 760px; padding: 72px 0 120px; }
  .eyebrow { color: #d7f96a; }
  .eyebrow span { display: inline-block; margin-right: 9px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 7rem); letter-spacing: -0.1em; line-height: 0.9; margin: 28px 0 18px; }
  .updated { margin: 0; }
  .lead { color: #f1efe7; font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 64px 0 0; }
  section { border-top: 1px solid #373832; margin-top: 54px; padding-top: 18px; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -0.05em; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  p { color: #aaa9a0; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  section a { color: #d7f96a; }
  .footer-note { align-items: end; border-top: 1px solid #373832; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 22px 0 34px; }
  .footer-note p { color: #85867c; font-size: 0.78rem; margin: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .shell { width: min(100% - 32px, 1120px); }
    .policy-page { padding-top: 72px; }
    .lead { margin-top: 48px; }
    .footer-note { align-items: start; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }
  }
</style>
